**Usage:**
`    mdview [OPTIONS] HOMEPATH [HOMEPAGE [TITLE]]`
ATX3 
Press `[F1]` in the GUI viewer to open the Welcome Page and get more help. HBRK
`HOMEPATH` is the file or directory to open. `HOMEPAGE` is the file to open if HBRK
`HOMEPATH` is a directory. If `HOMEPAGE` is empty, DEFAULT_INDEX is used instead. HBRK
If `TITLE` is empty, DEFAULT_WINDOW_TITLE is used for the window title. HBRK
In Markdown, relative paths are based on the directory of the currently viewed HBRK
file. If this fails, the directory of the `HOMEPAGE` file is used.
ATX3 
ATX3 OUTPUT FORMATS
ATX3 
If an output format is not specified the file is opened in the GUI viewer. HBRK
Some formats can be tweaked (see section OUTPUT MODIFIERS).
ATX3 
`   --ansi               `Text with ANSI escape codes. HBRK
`   --bare               `Plain text with most Markdown formatting removed. HBRK
`   --html               `HTML fragment. HBRK
`   --text               `Decorated text. HBRK
#ifndef OPT_PANGO
`   --tty                `Text with vt100 codes.
#else
`   --tty                `Text with vt100 codes. HBRK
`   --pango              `Raw Pango markup (debug).
#endif
#ifdef OPT_MARKUP
ATX3 
ATX3 INPUT MODIFIERS
ATX3 
`   --markup=FILE        `Skip the parser and load Pango markup from FILE (debug).
#endif
ATX3 
ATX3 OUTPUT MODIFIERS
ATX3 
#ifndef COMMONMARK_FENCED_CODEBLOCK_LINE_ENDING
`   --cm-block-end       `Add an empty line at code block end. HBRK
#endif
`   --html-base=[DIR]    `Use `DIR` instead of `HOMEPATH` for the `<base>` tag. HBRK
`                      `Leave `DIR` empty to omit `<base>` tag and javascript. HBRK
`   --html-css=NUM       `Embed CSS style sheet NUM in 0..2; default 0 but in the HBRK
`                      `Viewer it is NUM=2 for HTML Preview. Implies `--html-full`. HBRK
`   --html-full          `Render a full HTML document, with a `<base>` tag to set HBRK
`                      `relative links to `HOMEPATH`, and javascript to assist HBRK
`                      `internal links. See also the `--html-base` option. HBRK
`   --html5              `Output HTML5 rather than XHTML. HBRK
`   --output=FILE        `Redirect output to file `FILE`. HBRK
`   --soft-break         `Render line endings within input paragraphs as new lines HBRK
`                      `instead of joining input lines together. HBRK
`                      `Soft breaks can inhibit some smart text replacements. HBRK
`   --soft-break-br      `Append a hard break after a soft break in HTML output. HBRK
`   --unsafe-html        `Include raw HTML in all output formats.
ATX3 
ATX3 EXTENSIONS
ATX3 
`   --auto-lang          `If a link points to "F.ext", and "F`.$LANG`.ext" exists, HBRK
`                      `open the latter. This feature requires the Viewer. HBRK
`   --no-auto-code       `Disable rendering certain plain words as code spans. HBRK
`   --no-extensions      `Disable all extensions. HBRK
`   --no-heading-link    `Do not add heading anchors. This feature requires either HBRK
`                      `Viewer or HTML output. HBRK
`   --no-permlink        `Disable permissive auto-links. HBRK
`   --no-shebang         `Disable file shebang detection. HBRK
`   --no-smart           `Disable smart text replacements. HBRK
`   --no-strikethrough   `Disable support for striking text. HBRK
`   --no-table           `Disable support for Markdown tables. HBRK
`   --toc-level=LEVEL    `Replace the first occurrence of "`<!--[toc]-->`" with HBRK
`                      `the Table of Contents. If the pattern is missing, place HBRK
`                      `the ToC at the top. LEVEL in 0..6. This feature requires HBRK
`                      `heading link anchors, and either Viewer or HTML output.
ATX3 
ATX3 MISCELLANEOUS
ATX3 
`   --dump-css=NUM       `Output CSS style-sheet NUM and exit. HBRK
#ifdef OPT_EXIT_TEST
`   --exit-test          `Exit the viewer immediately after entering GTK main loop. HBRK
#endif
`   -h, --help           `Print this help page and exit. HBRK
`   --license            `Print the program license and exit. HBRK
`   --lint               `Enable the linter; needs either Viewer or HTML output. HBRK
`   --version            `Print the program version and exit.
ATX3 
ATX3 ENVIRONMENT
ATX3 
Program options can also be set using the environment variable `MDVIEW_OPTIONS`. HBRK
A command-line option will override any option with the same name set through HBRK
this variable. However, if `MDVIEW_OPTIONS` specifies `HOMEPATH`, `HOMEPAGE`, or HBRK
`TITLE`, these values will take precedence over their command-line counterparts.
ATX3 

#ifdef OPT_PANGO

ATX3 UNDOCUMENTED
ATX3 
These options went away.
ATX3 
`   --no-ext             `Combine `--no-auto-code`, `--no-permlink`, `--no-shebang` HBRK
`                      `and `--no-table`. HBRK
`   --soft-breaks        `
ATX3 
These internal options were never documented. Read the source code.
ATX3 
`   --emask=EMASK        ` HBRK
`   --tmask=TMASK        `
ATX3 
 `THE END`
/*
This file complies with the format recommended by `info help2man`:
  - Two spaces before an option; at least two spaces after the option.
  - "Usage:" written the way it is.
Due to the code span rules (see <https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/#code-spans>
and example 330), the code spans for options must begin with three spaces and
conclude with at least three spaces. Additionally, the leading code spans
of continuation lines that follow an option must end two columns before the
option's span. In summary, backticks should be placed in columns 1, 24 (for
continuation), and 26 (for the option).
*/
/*
Smart text works better without soft breaks because the absence of line
breaks allows pairing quotes across the whole paragraph. Instead, with
soft breaks enabled, quotes can only be paired together if they sit
in the same line.
*/
#endif
